    "summary": "Canoe shaped bowl of alder, raised ends, flared sides, lines of fine knife work decoration on the inside - vertical at the ends, horizontal on the sides, and oblique across the bottom. The flat edge is inlaid with univalve opercula. The bowl has a long split in the base and one side, with native repairs consisting of pegged, countersunk, stitches, using root or withe as thread, and, at the sides copper nails or pegs.",
